------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NAMING  (Honesty #9 No-silent-drift — documented)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The public view is `FormLabel`, NOT `Label`. `Label` is a SwiftUI built-in used at 14 call sites in this
module (`Label(_, systemImage:)` in AppShell/States/Lists/Playback/PushDemoView/… + `.labelStyle(...)`);
declaring a module-level `Label` would SHADOW the built-in and break those call sites — introducing FOREIGN
red attributable to this work, which is forbidden. `FormLabel` also matches the web source's own note:
"the Typography Label re-exported from @/components/ui is a span-based typography role — semantically
distinct from this form label." The diagnostics surface slug stays "Label" (per the prompt). All other
types are `Label`-prefixed and collide with nothing in SwiftUI (LabelSurface/Input/Projection/Projector/
Model/Strings/Telemetry/Resolve/Body/RequiredMarker).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing / #5 No-parity-shortcuts)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <Label> is a PURE presentational PRIMITIVE. It renders an HTML <label> around caller-supplied
`children` and, when `required`, appends a red `*` (aria-hidden="true", className="text-rose-300") plus a
<VisuallyHidden> ${t('form.required','required')} so the paired control's accessible name reads
"<label> required" (WCAG 3.3.2). Its inputs are plain props (children, required, the pass-through htmlFor +
className). There is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise -> therefore NO loading / error / stale /
offline branch (there is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect from; the host owns the field's data
states). Reproducing those generic states would FABRICATE behaviour the source does not have, so this
surface reproduces only the source's REAL branches — exactly the disposition the accepted sibling
presentational primitives Delta (0081), MetricCard (0095), InlineCallout (0124), ActiveFilterChips (0147),
StaggerItem (0194), and Accordion (0203) used. The REAL branches, all reproduced + tested:
  • not-required        : the label text alone (web `<label>{children}</label>`).
  • required            : text + visible `*` (statusDanger, VoiceOver-hidden) AND the spoken "required"
                          folded into the accessible name ("<label> required") — the native peer of the
                          web aria-hidden `*` + the visually-hidden ` required` (WCAG 3.3.2).
  • field association   : the optional fieldIdentifier (web htmlFor) surfaced as the accessibility id.
  • empty-text leaf     : the native never-a-blank-box peer of an empty `<label>` — a muted fallback
                          ("Unlabeled field"); the `*` still renders when required.
Data source  : useTranslation (web) -> the P1/S10 LabelStrings facade; no fetch (pure presentational).
Shared comps : @/components/a11y VisuallyHidden -> reproduced natively as accessibilityHidden(* glyph) +
               the composed accessibilityLabel carrying the spoken "required" (the idiomatic SwiftUI peer
               of a visually-hidden span; no separate hidden element needed).
Charts/maps  : none (the web source uses none) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : form.required (the ONLY web key, mirrored verbatim: t('form.required','required')) + the
               native addition label.empty; both resolve through the P1/S10 facade. No English literals
               in Swift code.
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "Label" (P1/S11).
a11y         : the label is ONE VoiceOver element whose name is "<text>" / "<text> required"; the `*` glyph
               is accessibilityHidden; fieldIdentifier -> accessibilityIdentifier (web htmlFor); Dynamic
               Type via the design tokens; no motion (nothing to reduce).

